WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.520
The team runs on AWS.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.030
Your last job was on another cloud.

3
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.580
Senior loops assume you can build on any cloud.

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.540
The ideas are the same.

5
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:15.615
Four areas: the data lake, access and network, code for infrastructure, and cost.

6
00:00:15.635 --> 00:00:18.450
First: the data lake on object storage.

7
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.600
S 3 stores objects under keys.

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.660
It has no real folders.

9
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.910
So a rename is a copy and a delete, for every object.

10
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.145
On big data, that is slow.

11
00:00:28.165 --> 00:00:31.445
A catalog, like Glue, maps those files to tables.

12
00:00:31.465 --> 00:00:34.570
Then Athena or Spark can query them.

13
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.530
Second: who can read what?

14
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.293
Give a job a role, not a key.

15
00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:41.140
A role hands out short-lived credentials.

16
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.590
And grant least privilege.

17
00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.540
Only this bucket.

18
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.950
Only read.

19
00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.425
Keep traffic to storage on a private endpoint.

20
00:00:47.445 --> 00:00:50.400
It is safer, and it is cheaper.

21
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.760
Third: no clicks in the console.

22
00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.048
With Terraform, buckets, roles and clusters are code.

23
00:00:56.068 --> 00:00:58.220
You review them like any change.

24
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.508
Docker packs a job with its libraries.

25
00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:02.955
So it runs the same way everywhere.

26
00:01:02.975 --> 00:01:05.917
And a CI pipeline tests and ships each change.

27
00:01:05.937 --> 00:01:08.480
No one deploys by hand.

28
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.615
Last: why did the bill jump?

29
00:01:10.635 --> 00:01:13.790
Look at three places first: compute that never stops,

30
00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.365
data that crosses regions, and old storage.

31
00:01:17.385 --> 00:01:19.950
Quick recap of cloud and DevOps.

32
00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.887
Object storage has no rename.

33
00:01:21.907 --> 00:01:23.550
Use roles, not keys.

34
00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.735
And keep infrastructure in code.

35
00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:28.855
Now start the first lesson below.
